# Minecraft Fabric Mod Project

This is a Minecraft Fabric mod project template with automated builds, testing, and documentation.

## Project Structure

### Core Mod Files
- `build.gradle` - Main build configuration for Fabric mod
- `gradle.properties` - Project properties and version definitions
- `settings.gradle` - Gradle project settings with Fabric repository
- `src/main/java/com/khazoda/basicstorage/BasicStorage.java` - Main mod entry point
- `src/main/java/com/khazoda/basicstorage/BasicStorageClient.java` - Client entry point

### Resources
- `src/main/resources/fabric.mod.json` - Fabric mod metadata
- `src/main/resources/data/basicstorage/recipes/` - Recipe definitions
- `src/main/resources/assets/basicstorage/lang/` - Localization files
- `src/main/resources/assets/basicstorage/textures/` - Texture assets
- `src/main/resources/assets/basicstorage/models/` - Model files
- `src/main/resources/basic-storage.mixins.json` - Mixin configuration

### Build & CI/CD
- `build.ps1` - PowerShell build script for local development (Windows)
- `.github/workflows/build.yml` - GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline (if configured)

### Java Package Structure
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage` - Main package
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.block` - Block implementations
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.item` - Item implementations
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.registry` - Registry classes
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.storage` - Storage system
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.util` - Utility classes
- `com.khazoda.basicstorage.datagen` - Data generation

## Key Technical Details
- **Minecraft Version**: 1.21
- **Fabric Loader**: 0.16.9+
- **Fabric API**: 0.102.0+1.21
- **Java Version**: 21
- **Gradle**: Latest with Fabric Loom
- **Mod ID**: basicstorage
- **Maven Group**: com.khazoda

## Development Workflow
1. Configure mod properties in `gradle.properties`
2. Implement mod functionality in Java classes
3. Add recipes, textures, and other assets
4. Test locally using `.\build.ps1` or `./gradlew runClient`
5. Build mod JAR with `.\build.ps1` or `./gradlew build`
6. Create releases using Git tags
7. CI/CD automatically publishes to GitHub and Modrinth (if configured)

